WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.102
-How are you doing?
How's the family doing?

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.037
How are the kids?
-They're getting bigger.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.072
-They are.
-That's what happens.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.172
Yeah, it turns out they grow.

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:08.674
-How old's the baby now.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.075
-He's two and a half.
-Oh, he's so cute.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:11.411
-Yeah, he's so cute.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.146
He's so cute.
Yeah, everybody's good.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.247
-Does he know about
Christmas really yet or not?

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.617
-Um, I've been trying to,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.019
like, kind of, like,
lead him towards that.

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:23.389
We've been watching the Rudolph
claymation thing a lot.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.658
-Yeah, that's good.
-And yeah, he likes it.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.927
He's like "Oh, Rudolph."
-Yeah.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.529
He's already into that.
-He loves him.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.898
-Does your daughter have
a list of toys and things?

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:35.935
-She does have a list
of toys and things,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:39.172
but they're pretty specific.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.975
So she'll be --
she'll be like, I want --

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:45.645
Okay, I want a dress.
It's fluffy on the top,

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.047
and then on the sides,
it's got like, little sequins.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.649
I'm like, what is this thing?
-It's very specific.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.184
-Yeah, yeah,
it's like too specific.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.954
-Were you like that as a kid?
-Um, no.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.423
I mean, I, like, my best

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.293
if I think about, like,
my favorite thing I ever got,

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:05.965
I got a "Jurassic Park"
pup tent that I slept in

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.068
for like six months
in my bedroom on the floor.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.736
-So a tent on the floor?
-Yeah.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.106
My sister was not as happy about
it because we shared a room,

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:16.943
but yes, I pitched a tent
in our -- in our bedroom

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.145
and slept on the hard floor,
comfortably

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.148
slept on the hard floor because
we had like no bones back then

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.850
or I don't know what.
-We did that all the time, too.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.418
We would ask to sleep
on the floor.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.753
-Why didn't it hurt then?
-It was a treat.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:27.920
-I don't understand.
-We had a sleeping bag.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.355
We'd be like, mom,
can we -- could me

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.190
and Gloria just like
camp out in the living room?

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.026
-I feel like if I slept
on the floor now,

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.027
I would, like, disintegrate.
-I know.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.729
-I would just turn into --

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.631
I'd be like, boneless
when I woke up, yeah.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.700
-That's true really funny,
-Yeah.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.935
-I wanted to ask you something.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.770
This is a clip that's viral.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.338
A clip of you being interviewed
on the red carpet.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.007
This is in 2006...
-Oh, God.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.408
-...and I don't,
if you remember this story,

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.843
but a woman walked --
-Is it offensive? What did I do?

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.378
-No, no no, no.
It's cool. No, no, it's cool.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:57.050
A woman walks behind you, and it
looks like she fully disappears.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.484
Do you know
what I'm talking about?

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.085
-No.
-Watch this video.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.287
This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.623 line:0%
-And what was the highlight
of the evening for you tonight?

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.258
-Philip Seymour Hoffman

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:10.997
winning for best actor
for a drama.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:14.333
Oh, my God,
that -- that is my mom.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.168
That is my mom.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:19.072
-Wait. What?
-That's my mom.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.140
-Wait, let's watch it again.
That's your mom? But what...?

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.441 line:0%
-That woman with the dark hair?
-Yes.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.776 line:0%
-Is my mother.

00:02:23.842 --> 00:02:25.277 line:0%
-That's your mom?
-That's my mom, yes.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.647
-Philip Seymour Hoffman winning
for best actor for a drama.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:31.017
-And where...?

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:32.885
-I've been looking for her for,
like, the last 15 years.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.288
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.324
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.426
-You are the best.

00:02:40.492 --> 00:02:42.462
That is so funny.
-That is very strange.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.097
-That's your mom?
-That is fully my mom.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.934
-Hi, mom. That's so cute.
-That is weird.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.369
Where did she go?
-[ Laughs ]

